  "question": {
    "text": "In which of the following octahedral complex species the magnitude of $\\Delta_0$ will be maximum?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3cZK2",
      "text": "\n$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\right)_6\\right]^{2+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZCjbt",
      "text": "\n$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "P531E",
      "text": "\n$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4\\right)_3\\right]^{3-}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8UW65",
      "text": "\n$\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{3+}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Crystal field splitting depends upon the nature of ligand. The nature of ligand $\\Delta$ decreases as shown below\n$\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4^{--} < \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} < \\mathrm{NH}_3 < \\mathrm{CN}^{-}$\nhence the crystal field splitting will be maximum for $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}$",
    "image": null
